---
// How agents work on the plan: criteria and a plan first, then claim, ask and prove, with the person in charge.
import Screenshot from "../Screenshot.astro";
import claimLight from "../../assets/screens/android-claim-light.webp";
import claimDark from "../../assets/screens/android-claim-dark.webp";
import approvalLight from "../../assets/screens/android-approval-light.webp";
import approvalDark from "../../assets/screens/android-approval-dark.webp";
import proofLight from "../../assets/screens/android-proof-light.webp";
import proofDark from "../../assets/screens/android-proof-dark.webp";
import agentsLight from "../../assets/screens/android-agents-light.webp";
import agentsDark from "../../assets/screens/android-agents-dark.webp";
import notification from "../../assets/screens/android-notification-light.webp";
import historyLight from "../../assets/screens/mac-history-light.webp";
import historyDark from "../../assets/screens/mac-history-dark.webp";

const phoneWidths = [300, 600, 900];
---

<section id="agents" aria-labelledby="agents-title">
  <h2 id="agents-title">Built for agents, with you in charge</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    Any MCP client, or any agent that can run a command, works on the same plan you do. Here is one made-up day of
    that work.
  </p>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="row-text">
      <h3>Say what done means</h3>
      <p>
        Give a task acceptance criteria, a plan and a note before the work starts. The agent reads them over MCP or
        with <code>dayhand show</code>, ticks each criterion as it meets it and leaves the note where it stopped.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="terminal wrap">
      <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
      <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="The dayhand show command printing one task"><code><span class="prompt">$</span> dayhand show 12
<span class="out">#12 Publish the October newsletter
status   todo
due      2026-10-24 17:00 (today)
labels   marketing
claimed  claude until 2026-10-24 19:01
id       m97akk9x3n5fd3j4fbdva7jf818gxt1v
acceptance:
  1. [x] Every link opens
  2. [x] The unsubscribe link works
  3. [ ] You approved the final text
plan:
  Draft it from this month's notes, check every link, then ask before sending
note:
  The draft is in newsletter-october.md.</span></code></pre>
      <figcaption>One task as <code>dayhand show</code> prints it; the change history that follows is cut here.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <ol class="strip story" role="list" aria-label="Claim, ask and prove, on Android; scrolls sideways" tabindex="0">
    <li>
      <figure class="shot">
        <Screenshot
          class="phone"
          light={claimLight}
          dark={claimDark}
          widths={phoneWidths}
          sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 17rem, 72vw"
          alt="The task Update the pricing page on Android, in progress, with the line agent: claude works until 19:01, and its acceptance criteria, one of two met."
        />
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Claim.</strong> claude holds this task until 19:01, so no other agent can change it. When the time
          runs out, anyone may take it; your own changes always go through.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </li>
    <li>
      <figure class="shot">
        <Screenshot
          class="phone"
          light={approvalLight}
          dark={approvalDark}
          widths={phoneWidths}
          sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 17rem, 72vw"
          alt="An approval request on Android: claude asks to send the October newsletter to the mailing list, which cannot be undone, with a deadline and two answers, Send now and Keep it as a draft."
        />
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Ask.</strong> Before a step that cannot be undone, the agent asks and waits. You pick an answer;
          with none by the deadline, the request expires and the agent is told.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </li>
    <li>
      <figure class="shot">
        <Screenshot
          class="phone"
          light={proofLight}
          dark={proofDark}
          widths={phoneWidths}
          sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 17rem, 72vw"
          alt="The finished task Export the Q3 sales report on Android, with both acceptance criteria met and the proof of completion: three CSV files are in reports/q3 and the totals match the bank statement, with two passed checks."
        />
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Prove.</strong> A task with criteria is done only when they are met and the agent says what it did,
          with named checks such as <code>totals=pass</code>.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="row-text">
      <h3>You set the rules</h3>
      <p>
        One switch pauses every agent. A policy for each agent key allows, asks for or denies each tool, and work an
        agent proposes waits in an inbox until you accept, merge or reject it. A health card above Today shows what
        needs a look.
      </p>
      <p>
        The phone checks for new approval requests about every 15 minutes and shows them as a notification. Dayhand
        uses no push service, so nothing sits between your server and your phone.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row-media stack">
      <Screenshot
        class="notice"
        light={notification}
        widths={[500, 996]}
        sizes="(min-width: 30rem) 22rem, calc(100vw - 2rem)"
        alt="An Android notification from Dayhand: claude asks for your approval, Send the October newsletter to the mailing list."
      />
      <Screenshot
        class="phone"
        light={agentsLight}
        dark={agentsDark}
        widths={phoneWidths}
        sizes="17rem"
        alt="The Agents screen on Android: the Pause agents switch, one request waiting for you, one proposal from claude, and tool policies that deny delete_task to bookkeeper and claude and ask before claude completes a task."
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row wide">
    <div class="row-text">
      <h3>See who did what</h3>
      <p>
        Every person and every agent key signs its changes, so an agent's edits stand out in the task history and the
        activity log, and <code>dayhand log --by agent</code> lists them in the terminal. Revoke a key and that agent
        is out.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Screenshot
      class="window"
      light={historyLight}
      dark={historyDark}
      widths={[700, 1080, 1600, 2160]}
      sizes="(min-width: 72rem) 70rem, calc(100vw - 2rem)"
      alt="Dayhand for macOS with the history of Write the case study for the logo project, newest first: the agent claude moved it to in progress, added a note, ticked two checklist items and claimed it, after you created it from the command line."
    />
  </div>

  <div class="connect">
    <h3>Connect an agent</h3>
    <p>
      The server speaks MCP at <code>/mcp</code>. Any MCP client connects with the address and an
      <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> header; for Claude Code it is one command. The Claude apps connect as a custom
      connector with OAuth, and you approve each connection on your phone.
    </p>
    <p>
      Agents that run shell commands use <code>dayhand</code>. With <code>--json</code> it prints exactly what the MCP
      tools return, and a ready Agent Skill teaches an agent the commands.
    </p>
    <pre tabindex="0" class="code" data-copy data-copy-label="Copy the commands that connect Claude Code"><code>AGENT_KEY=$(dayhand key create claude --scope write --json | jq -r .key)
claude mcp add --transport http dayhand http://127.0.0.1:3211/mcp \
  --header "Authorization: Bearer $AGENT_KEY"</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p class="note">
    Dayhand records your decisions and the agents' work in the plan. It cannot stop what an agent does outside
    Dayhand.
  </p>
</section>
